From: Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 08:20:50 -0700
Subject: Prevent UAF during re-entrant destruction in IME callouts.

During IME callouts (such as SetVirtualKeyboardVisibilityIfEnabled or
NotifySelectionBoundsChanged), the RenderWidgetHostViewAura or the
updated view can be re-entrantly destroyed or unregistered. This CL adds
weak pointer checks and re-fetches the text input state after these
callouts to prevent accessing freed memory. A unit test is added to
verify the fix when destruction occurs during virtual keyboard
visibility updates.

Bug: 553133215
Change-Id: I4a6fc2c50133c731dad652c07906e6aa597c82dc
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8351288
Reviewed-by: Kartar Singh <kartarsingh@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694603}

